ation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"internal/sbi/server.go","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":73,"endLine":90,"snippet":{"text":"\tbindAddr := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s:%d\", sbiConfig.BindingIPv4, sbiConfig.Port)"},"startColumn":2,"startLine":90}}}],"message":{"text":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf($XX, bindAddr)\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"8105be690700da1f0737c7d7c4a992bd0470379d56e0721c220f3bc5f7ce52c49b0fe771ceeaea77a49b3e3f5a8c7d99fe9f0b5c8a35ffe764d2db557bc9203b_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"internal/sbi/server.go","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":73,"endLine":90,"snippet":{"text":"\tbindAddr := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s:%d\", sbiConfig.BindingIPv4, sbiConfig.Port)"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":90}}}],"message":{"text":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf(sbiConfig.BindingIPv4, sbiConfig.Port)\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"5b55ef95c07d186edd4734b9e05c9cd6afbb41c3e5ecb3687efc79a3cc4905311d52007702761dac8b89ac9e6aa6b9b73a4f8041398dae187fdfad1bc5545b0d_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"internal/sbi/server.go","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":73,"endLine":90,"snippet":{"text":"\tbindAddr := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s:%d\", sbiConfig.BindingIPv4, sbiConfig.Port)"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":90}}}],"message":{"text":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf(sbiConfig.Port, sbiConfig.BindingIPv4)\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port"}],"tool":{"driver":{"name":"Semgrep PRO","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Consider to use well-defined context"},"help":{"markdown":"Consider to use well-defined context\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/dgryski.semgrep-go.contexttodo.context-todo)\n","text":"Consider to use well-defined context"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/dgryski.semgrep-go.contexttodo.context-todo","id":"dgryski.semgrep-go.contexttodo.context-todo","name":"dgryski.semgrep-go.contexttodo.context-todo","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["global-policy"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: dgryski.semgrep-go.contexttodo.context-todo"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf($XX, $NET)\n"},"help":{"markdown":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf($XX, $NET)\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port)\n","text":"use net.JoinHostPort instead of fmt.Sprintf($XX, $NET)\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port","id":"dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port","name":"dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["global-policy"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: dgryski.semgrep-go.hostport.sprintf-host-port"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Do not use `math/rand`. Use `crypto/rand` instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Do not use `math/rand`. Use `crypto/rand` instead.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/go.lang.security.audit.crypto.math_random.math-random-used)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#secure-random-number-generation](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#secure-random-number-generation)\n","text":"Do not use `math/rand`. Use `crypto/rand` instead."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/go.lang.security.audit.crypto.math_random.math-random-used","id":"go.lang.security.audit.crypto.math_random.math-random-used","name":"go.lang.security.audit.crypto.math_random.math-random-used","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","global-policy","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: go.lang.security.audit.crypto.math_random.math-random-used"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data / Improper Preservation of Permissions. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent silently dropped key constraint extensions (e.g. restrict-destination-v00@openssh.com) when forwarding keys to a remote agent, and the in-memory keyring silently ignored unsupported constraint extensions instead of rejecting them. A forwarded key intended to be restricted could therefore be used without its constraints, letting an attacker who controls the remote/jump host abuse the key against any destination it trusts."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data / Improper Preservation of Permissions. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent silently dropped key constraint extensions (e.g. restrict-destination-v00@openssh.com) when forwarding keys to a remote agent, and the in-memory keyring silently ignored unsupported constraint extensions instead of rejecting them. A forwarded key intended to be restricted could therefore be used without its constraints, letting an attacker who controls the remote/jump host abuse the key against any destination it trusts.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-02ef276f-345d-4a72-a219-2c2d913c01ad)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31390](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31390)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f5wc-c3c7-36mc](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f5wc-c3c7-36mc)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39832](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39832)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data / Improper Preservation of Permissions. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent silently dropped key constraint extensions (e.g. restrict-destination-v00@openssh.com) when forwarding keys to a remote agent, and the in-memory keyring silently ignored unsupported constraint extensions instead of rejecting them. A forwarded key intended to be restricted could therefore be used without its constraints, letting an attacker who controls the remote/jump host abuse the key against any destination it trusts."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-02ef276f-345d-4a72-a219-2c2d913c01ad","id":"ssc-02ef276f-345d-4a72-a219-2c2d913c01ad","name":"ssc-02ef276f-345d-4a72-a219-2c2d913c01ad","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-281: Improper Preservation of Permissions","CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A08:2017 - Insecure Deserialization","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-02ef276f-345d-4a72-a219-2c2d913c01ad"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Type Conversion or Cast. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can send a well-crafted SSH packet that triggers an out-of-bounds slice panic in the AES-GCM packet decoder of golang.org/x/crypto/ssh, crashing the process (denial of service). AES-GCM is a default cipher, so the vulnerable decode path is reached whenever an SSH client or server connection is established with ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, or ssh.NewServerConn."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Type Conversion or Cast. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can send a well-crafted SSH packet that triggers an out-of-bounds slice panic in the AES-GCM packet decoder of golang.org/x/crypto/ssh, crashing the process (denial of service). AES-GCM is a default cipher, so the vulnerable decode path is reached whenever an SSH client or server connection is established with ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, or ssh.NewServerConn.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-315b77ec-61d5-4592-a479-115d5df00452)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31388](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31388)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q4h4-gmj2-qvw2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q4h4-gmj2-qvw2)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46597](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46597)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Type Conversion or Cast. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can send a well-crafted SSH packet that triggers an out-of-bounds slice panic in the AES-GCM packet decoder of golang.org/x/crypto/ssh, crashing the process (denial of service). AES-GCM is a default cipher, so the vulnerable decode path is reached whenever an SSH client or server connection is established with ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, or ssh.NewServerConn."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-315b77ec-61d5-4592-a479-115d5df00452","id":"ssc-315b77ec-61d5-4592-a479-115d5df00452","name":"ssc-315b77ec-61d5-4592-a479-115d5df00452","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-704: Incorrect Type Conversion or Cast","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-315b77ec-61d5-4592-a479-115d5df00452"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization / Incorrect Implementation of Authentication Algorithm. The golang.org/x/crypto/ssh server only enforced the \"source-address\" critical option on the public-key authentication path. When an SSH session authenticated through a non-public-key callback (password, keyboard-interactive, or GSSAPI-with-MIC) returns an ssh.Permissions value carrying a \"source-address\" critical option, the source-address restriction is silently skipped, allowing a client from a disallowed network to bypass the intended authorization control."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization / Incorrect Implementation of Authentication Algorithm. The golang.org/x/crypto/ssh server only enforced the \"source-address\" critical option on the public-key authentication path. When an SSH session authenticated through a non-public-key callback (password, keyboard-interactive, or GSSAPI-with-MIC) returns an ssh.Permissions value carrying a \"source-address\" critical option, the source-address restriction is silently skipped, allowing a client from a disallowed network to bypass the intended authorization control.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-63089c4e-55d0-401e-a63c-5aa02708bc94)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31398](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31398)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x527-x647-q7gg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x527-x647-q7gg)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45337](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45337)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46595](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46595)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization / Incorrect Implementation of Authentication Algorithm. The golang.org/x/crypto/ssh server only enforced the \"source-address\" critical option on the public-key authentication path. When an SSH session authenticated through a non-public-key callback (password, keyboard-interactive, or GSSAPI-with-MIC) returns an ssh.Permissions value carrying a \"source-address\" critical option, the source-address restriction is silently skipped, allowing a client from a disallowed network to bypass the intended authorization control."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-63089c4e-55d0-401e-a63c-5aa02708bc94","id":"ssc-63089c4e-55d0-401e-a63c-5aa02708bc94","name":"ssc-63089c4e-55d0-401e-a63c-5aa02708bc94","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-303: Incorrect Implementation of Authentication Algorithm","CWE-863: Incorrect Authorization","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-63089c4e-55d0-401e-a63c-5aa02708bc94"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Integer Overflow or Wraparound. An integer truncation in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh causes the internal payload-size calculation to overflow when a single Write (or WriteExtended) call on an SSH channel carries more than 4GB of data, making the write loop spin forever while sending empty packets. This affects any application that establishes an SSH client or server connection (ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, ssh.NewServerConn) and then writes a large payload to a channel or session."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Integer Overflow or Wraparound. An integer truncation in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh causes the internal payload-size calculation to overflow when a single Write (or WriteExtended) call on an SSH channel carries more than 4GB of data, making the write loop spin forever while sending empty packets. This affects any application that establishes an SSH client or server connection (ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, ssh.NewServerConn) and then writes a large payload to a channel or session.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-6bce5557-ea37-4670-b3c1-def6e1e7b6cb)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31400](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31400)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rm3j-f69w-wqmq](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rm3j-f69w-wqmq)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39834](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39834)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Integer Overflow or Wraparound. An integer truncation in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh causes the internal payload-size calculation to overflow when a single Write (or WriteExtended) call on an SSH channel carries more than 4GB of data, making the write loop spin forever while sending empty packets. This affects any application that establishes an SSH client or server connection (ssh.Dial, ssh.NewClientConn, ssh.NewServerConn) and then writes a large payload to a channel or session."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-6bce5557-ea37-4670-b3c1-def6e1e7b6cb","id":"ssc-6bce5557-ea37-4670-b3c1-def6e1e7b6cb","name":"ssc-6bce5557-ea37-4670-b3c1-def6e1e7b6cb","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-190: Integer Overflow or Wraparound","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-6bce5557-ea37-4670-b3c1-def6e1e7b6cb"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer / Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. A malicious SSH peer can send unsolicited global request responses that accumulate in the connection multiplexer's bounded internal buffer, blocking the connection's read loop. The blocked goroutine cannot be released even after calling Close(), causing a per-connection goroutine and memory leak (denial of service). Any SSH client or server connection established with golang.org/x/crypto/ssh reaches the vulnerable multiplexer."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer / Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. A malicious SSH peer can send unsolicited global request responses that accumulate in the connection multiplexer's bounded internal buffer, blocking the connection's read loop. The blocked goroutine cannot be released even after calling Close(), causing a per-connection goroutine and memory leak (denial of service). Any SSH client or server connection established with golang.org/x/crypto/ssh reaches the vulnerable multiplexer.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-8c39b516-d6be-4e51-afa4-055a3dc56da7)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31397](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31397)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vgwf-h737-ff37](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vgwf-h737-ff37)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39830](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39830)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer / Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime. A malicious SSH peer can send unsolicited global request responses that accumulate in the connection multiplexer's bounded internal buffer, blocking the connection's read loop. The blocked goroutine cannot be released even after calling Close(), causing a per-connection goroutine and memory leak (denial of service). Any SSH client or server connection established with golang.org/x/crypto/ssh reaches the vulnerable multiplexer."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-8c39b516-d6be-4e51-afa4-055a3dc56da7","id":"ssc-8c39b516-d6be-4e51-afa4-055a3dc56da7","name":"ssc-8c39b516-d6be-4e51-afa4-055a3dc56da7","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer","CWE-772: Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-8c39b516-d6be-4e51-afa4-055a3dc56da7"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. The in-memory keyring returned by golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent's NewKeyring() silently accepts keys with ConfirmBeforeUse set to true but never enforces the constraint. A key that the developer expects to require user confirmation before each use will instead sign operations without any confirmation, defeating the intended access control on that key."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. The in-memory keyring returned by golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent's NewKeyring() silently accepts keys with ConfirmBeforeUse set to true but never enforces the constraint. A key that the developer expects to require user confirmation before each use will instead sign operations without any confirmation, defeating the intended access control on that key.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-913e8f3a-f9f6-4d0f-aa1c-c166c69715d1)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31389](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31389)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jppx-rxg9-jmrx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jppx-rxg9-jmrx)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39833](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39833)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. The in-memory keyring returned by golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent's NewKeyring() silently accepts keys with ConfirmBeforeUse set to true but never enforces the constraint. A key that the developer expects to require user confirmation before each use will instead sign operations without any confirmation, defeating the intended access control on that key."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-913e8f3a-f9f6-4d0f-aa1c-c166c69715d1","id":"ssc-913e8f3a-f9f6-4d0f-aa1c-c166c69715d1","name":"ssc-913e8f3a-f9f6-4d0f-aa1c-c166c69715d1","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-862: Missing Authorization","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-913e8f3a-f9f6-4d0f-aa1c-c166c69715d1"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts failed to validate the revocation status of a certificate authority SignatureKey, so an SSH host certificate signed by a @revoked CA was still accepted. Applications building a host key callback with knownhosts.New exercise the affected revocation-checking code path."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts failed to validate the revocation status of a certificate authority SignatureKey, so an SSH host certificate signed by a @revoked CA was still accepted. Applications building a host key callback with knownhosts.New exercise the affected revocation-checking code path.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-9ef5c35e-a137-440d-8d5a-ebfa9a39019b)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31399](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31399)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5cgq-3rg8-m6cv](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5cgq-3rg8-m6cv)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-42508](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-42508)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts failed to validate the revocation status of a certificate authority SignatureKey, so an SSH host certificate signed by a @revoked CA was still accepted. Applications building a host key callback with knownhosts.New exercise the affected revocation-checking code path."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-9ef5c35e-a137-440d-8d5a-ebfa9a39019b","id":"ssc-9ef5c35e-a137-440d-8d5a-ebfa9a39019b","name":"ssc-9ef5c35e-a137-440d-8d5a-ebfa9a39019b","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-9ef5c35e-a137-440d-8d5a-ebfa9a39019b"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not validate the User Presence flag when verifying FIDO/U2F security-key signatures (sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com and sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com), so signatures produced without a physical touch of the hardware key were accepted. Any code that runs the SSH handshake or verifies SSH certificates/host keys with this package reaches the flawed verification path."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not validate the User Presence flag when verifying FIDO/U2F security-key signatures (sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com and sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com), so signatures produced without a physical touch of the hardware key were accepted. Any code that runs the SSH handshake or verifies SSH certificates/host keys with this package reaches the flawed verification path.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-bd883eb0-57de-4dc1-abbe-b8099f45de65)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31395](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31395)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-89gr-r52h-f8rx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-89gr-r52h-f8rx)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39831](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39831)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Missing Authorization. golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not validate the User Presence flag when verifying FIDO/U2F security-key signatures (sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com and sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com), so signatures produced without a physical touch of the hardware key were accepted. Any code that runs the SSH handshake or verifies SSH certificates/host keys with this package reaches the flawed verification path."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-bd883eb0-57de-4dc1-abbe-b8099f45de65","id":"ssc-bd883eb0-57de-4dc1-abbe-b8099f45de65","name":"ssc-bd883eb0-57de-4dc1-abbe-b8099f45de65","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-862: Missing Authorization","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-bd883eb0-57de-4dc1-abbe-b8099f45de65"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input / Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. The RSA and DSA public key parsers in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not enforce size limits on key parameters. An attacker can supply a crafted public key with an excessively large RSA modulus or DSA parameter that causes several minutes of CPU consumption during signature verification, resulting in denial of service. This is reachable by unauthenticated clients during public key authentication."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input / Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. The RSA and DSA public key parsers in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not enforce size limits on key parameters. An attacker can supply a crafted public key with an excessively large RSA modulus or DSA parameter that causes several minutes of CPU consumption during signature verification, resulting in denial of service. This is reachable by unauthenticated clients during public key authentication.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e98e1c70-3cce-418d-961f-8b39587b8604)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31396](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31396)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w879-237q-wc7r](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w879-237q-wc7r)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39829](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39829)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input / Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature. The RSA and DSA public key parsers in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh did not enforce size limits on key parameters. An attacker can supply a crafted public key with an excessively large RSA modulus or DSA parameter that causes several minutes of CPU consumption during signature verification, resulting in denial of service. This is reachable by unauthenticated clients during public key authentication."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-e98e1c70-3cce-418d-961f-8b39587b8604","id":"ssc-e98e1c70-3cce-418d-961f-8b39587b8604","name":"ssc-e98e1c70-3cce-418d-961f-8b39587b8604","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-1284: Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input","CWE-347: Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-e98e1c70-3cce-418d-961f-8b39587b8604"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation / Improper Preservation of Permissions."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation / Improper Preservation of Permissions.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-0842aec4076a333089e2b007bc3520788cd47d1b)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31394](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31394)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-45gg-vh54-h5m9](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-45gg-vh54-h5m9)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39828](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39828)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/crypto are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation / Improper Preservation of Permissions."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-0842aec4076a333089e2b007bc3520788cd47d1b","id":"ssc-parity-0842aec4076a333089e2b007bc3520788cd47d1b","name":"ssc-parity-0842aec4076a333089e2b007bc3520788cd47d1b","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-281: Improper Preservation of Permissions","CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-parity-0842aec4076a333089e2b007bc3520788cd47d1b"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/net are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption."},"help":{"markdown":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/net are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-587e22a5b0de8ccfb3b54fd42c52234797c84552)\n - [https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31447](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-31447)\n - [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5cv4-jp36-h3mw](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5cv4-jp36-h3mw)\n - [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-25680](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-25680)\n","text":"Affected versions of golang.org/x/net are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Resource Consumption."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/orgs/-/supply-chain/advisories?q=ssc-parity-587e22a5b0de8ccfb3b54fd42c52234797c84552","id":"ssc-parity-587e22a5b0de8ccfb3b54fd42c52234797c84552","name":"ssc-parity-587e22a5b0de8ccfb3b54fd42c52234797c84552","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A06:2021 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: ssc-parity-587e22a5b0de8ccfb3b54fd42c52234797c84552"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Aff